  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multimodal multiprofile PCA + ResNet with avgpool and weighted fusion is the best configuration (0.639 accuracy, 0.620 F1), improving over RNA-only PCA avgpool and weak image-only ResNet models. A major remaining uncertainty is whether the image branch is limited by the ResNet encoder, since only ResNet has been tested for images. config_025 changes only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while keeping the proven multiprofile, avgpool, weighted-fusion, PCA-RNA setup. This cleanly tests whether a stronger image representation can improve the current best architecture and clarify whether image encoding is a key bottleneck. It is a high-value one-factor extension: it may yield immediate gains and, either way, tells us whether to invest further in image encoders or shift focus to RNA encoders and aggregation."
}

